==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Known since 1655, from {{der|en|la|alimōnia||food, support, nourishment, sustenance}} ({{cog|en|aliment}}, as in {{m|en|alimentary}}), itself from {{m|la|alo|alēre|to nourish}} + {{m|la|-mōnia||action, state, condition}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈæ.lɪ.mə.ni/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈæ.lɪ.moʊ.ni/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-alimony.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|alimonies}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} A [[court]]-[[mandate]]d [[allowance]] made to a [[former]] [[spouse]] by a [[divorce]]d or [[legally]] [[separated]] person.
# The [[means]] to [[support]] [[life]].

